# DEFECT 075: `acquires pclose` on `popen`, then `fclose`, was `check` 0 and
# `run` 0 on four platforms, and the child was never waited for
# (M-agreed-retention step 1, 2026-09-23). The named releaser was read for
# existence and never at the call that gave the handle back.
#
# The set now travels with the address: `p_open`'s mark says `p_close`, and a
# `consumes` call the mark did not name is stopped before C runs, which is why
# `C ran` never prints. The message says what the two declarations say and
# nothing about why they disagree.
extern "fixedbugs-a-release-the-mark-did-not-name-is-stopped-before-c.h"
    record H tag hh
    function p_open() -> H acquires p_close
    function p_close(x: H consumes)
    function h_close(x: H consumes)

function main()
    a = p_open()
    print("opened")
    h_close(x: a)
    print("not reached")
